Revision history for App::Mist

{{$NEXT}}

0.42 2026-06-06T11:22:11Z

  - merge: scope cpanm's --cascade-search to the mirror_only path so a sibling's
    declared version pin resolves from its mirror instead of failing on the
    consumer's stale copy; stays off live CPAN. Covered by t/merge-cascade.t.

0.41 2026-06-06T10:49:27Z

  - mpan-install: each install builds into its own copy-on-write generation
    (perl5/generations/<arch>-<counter>, hard-link seeded from the active one) and
    activates it by atomically repointing the perl5/<arch> symlink on success, so a
    failed install leaves the previous generation intact instead of bricking the env.
    Generations are kept, making rollback a single symlink repoint; a named --branch
    is a named generation. Covered by t/mpan-install-activation.t.

  - mpan-install: a failed build's staging dir is resumed by default on the next run
    (like re-running cpanm); --no-resume discards it and reseeds from the parent, and
    --rebuild skips the seed for an un-seeded clean room that sheds cruft a copy-on-
    write seed carries forward. The hard-link seed falls back to a full copy where
    hard links are unsupported (FAT, some network mounts).

  - mpan-install: perl5/bin/mist-run becomes a symlink to per-perl wrapper bodies
    (each sourcing its own rc), so building an alternate perl no longer hijacks the
    live wrapper and cross-perl switches are atomic. Adds --build-only (build without
    activating) and a switch-guard that prompts on a tty / refuses non-interactively
    before an implicit perl switch (--perlbrew=<ver> is the explicit confirmation).
    Covered by t/switch-verdict.t.

  - mpan-install: drop the --all-available-versions option - ambient (every perlbrew
    perl on the box, not project-scoped) and unused; build several perls with a caller
    loop over --perlbrew=<v> --build-only instead.

  - mpan-install: stamp `# Generated by App::Mist version <X>` at the top of the
    installer (after the shebang, mirrored in the VERSION POD), so which mist built a
    given mpan-install is readable at a glance.

0.40 2026-06-05T12:13:07Z

  - mist: add a git-style global -C <path> option that chdirs before the
    subcommand runs, so the project root and the perlbrew re-exec resolve from
    <path>. Repeatable (relative paths chain like git's), accepts -C path,
    -C=path and -Cpath. Covered by t/app-chdir-option.t.

0.39 2026-06-05T02:11:36Z

  - mist run: add --perlbrew=<ver> to run a command under the matching
    ./perl5/perl-<ver>-<arch>/ instead of the mistfile-pinned perl, for testing a
    dist against several perls built side by side; bypasses the version-pinned
    perl5/bin/mist-run wrapper.

  - mpan-install: sever non-tty STDIN before the perlbrew re-exec, so a
    from-scratch install in a background/CI/agent context no longer hangs on an
    inherited never-EOF pipe (a downstream read gets immediate EOF). Covered by
    t/script-perlbrew-stdin.t.

0.38 2026-06-02T20:53:23Z

  - release: add --candidate=<ID> to promote the build a --dry-run leaves behind,
    reusing its installed dependency closure (the slow part on a big release)
    instead of installing again; still bumps, rebuilds and retests. The candidate
    is fingerprint-guarded (refuses if cpanfile/mistfile/mpan-dist/perl changed)
    and ephemeral (each --dry-run wipes prior ones).

  - release: detect --dry-run the way Minilla does (Getopt auto_abbrev), so
    `mist release --dry` is treated as a dry run instead of running the trailing
    `dist` and leaving a tarball. The exact-string check missed abbreviations.

  - release POD: scope the hermeticity and non-interactive guarantees - the
    dist-test misses configure-time deps, and fail-fast covers only the changelog prompt.

  - index: fall back to META.json when a dist ships no META.yml, so a JSON-only
    dist's provides/no_index are honoured; dists shipping META.yml are unaffected.

  - mistfile DSL: `script` now accepts trailing arguments (`script $phase =>
    $path, @args`); its ($$) prototype had capped the verb at the path, leaving
    the body's @args (run by install.pm as system($path, @args)) unreachable -
    widened to ($$@). Also dropped assert's dead runtime coderef croak; its
    (&@) prototype already enforces a block at compile time.

0.37 2026-06-02T11:02:46Z

  - PackageIndex: order dist tarballs by numeric version components so a
    multi-digit point release sorts newest (1.9 < 1.10); version->parse read
    '1.10' as 1.1 and could attribute submodules to the older tarball. Handles
    v-strings and long CPAN::Meta versions; smoke-tested over mpan-dist.

  - release: install the dist's dependency closure into a throwaway contained
    lib and run the dist-test hermetically - a release never writes into (or can
    corrupt) mist's own perl5, and a dependency used but not declared in the
    cpanfile fails the dist-test instead of silently resolving from the shared
    perl5. Covered by t/release-cleanroom.t.

  - release: add --dry-run (build + clean-room dist-test, no bump/commit/tag/
    push). Both --dry-run and any non-interactive release now fail fast on a
    missing {{$NEXT}} changelog entry instead of hanging on Minilla's
    interactive edit-Changes prompt; an interactive release keeps the prompt.

  - Add a unit-test suite for the core logic: cpanm call-stack ordering
    (incl. the notest declaration-order invariant), mistfile DSL verbs + merge
    folding, Mist::Environment::as_code, the release changelog gate, the
    PAUSE-style module indexer (inline-version + POD-trap), mpan-dist tarball
    ordering/orphans, and Context::fetch_prereqs. ~200 assertions across t/.

  - MANIFEST.SKIP: anchor the `mistfile` skip to `^mistfile$` so t/mistfile.t and
    the t/share/mistfile.* fixtures ship in the dist; the release dist-test was
    silently NOTESTS (the unanchored pattern excluded the whole suite).

  - merge: print a 'mist compile' hint instead of $0's absolute path.

0.36 2026-05-28T18:54:57Z

  - release: skip Minilla's xt/ release-test generation by setting
    MINILLA_DISABLE_WRITE_RELEASE_TEST. POD/CPAN-Meta/spelling failures
    no longer interrupt the pipeline after the version bump; the
    clean-room t/ run against the extracted tarball is unaffected.

  - local_release + release: smart-bump heuristic. BumpVersion now
    consults `git ls-remote --exit-code origin refs/tags/<current>` and
    only bumps when the current source version's tag is on origin (i.e.
    already published). A local-only tag is treated as in-flight and the
    bump is skipped. Combined with TagLocal/TagPublish force-tagging, the
    intended workflow is:
      * cycle start (last release on origin) -> bump to next, tag locally
      * iterate via repeated local_release -> stay on the same version,
        tag moves to the current HEAD on each run
      * final mist release -> publish that exact version; the local tag
        is force-moved onto the release commit and pushed
    Previously every local_release auto-bumped (pseudo-releasing 0.36,
    0.37, 0.38, ... with no real-world presence), and then mist release
    skipped past the intended version entirely. Consumers vendoring the
    in-flight checkout via mist merge now see a stable version across
    iterations, so no consumer-side cpanfile re-bump is needed when the
    real release fires -- one final mist release in the source repo and
    every consumer is already in the right state.

  - local_release: no longer push the release commit or the new tag to
    origin, and no longer rewrites the {{$NEXT}} placeholder in Changes.
    The local release point is expected to be re-cut many times before
    it settles into something publishable -- pushing each intermediate
    state is wrong, and rewriting {{$NEXT}} on every run broke the next
    run's CheckChanges. The operator now drives the push explicitly, and
    Changes gets its definitive version+timestamp line only when the
    full `release` runs.

0.35 2026-05-22T03:25:25Z

  - release: seal the clean-room dist-test to the project's pinned
    mpan-dist mirror -- install with --mirror-only under $^X, without
    --with-develop, --notest for dependency suites, and RELEASE_TESTING
    cleared for the install. Ends live-CPAN leakage and the foreign-perl
    XS ABI crash during a release.
  - merge: resolve strictly from the pinned mpan mirrors, never live
    CPAN, so merging a sibling no longer drags the consumer's whole
    dependency closure forward.
  - notest: schedule notest modules in mistfile declaration order, not
    hash order, so a notest module that is a dependency of another can
    be listed first and installed --notest before the dependent.
  - mist-run: run the wrapped command directly instead of via perlbrew
    exec. perlbrew exec runs the command as a forked child and exits 1
    on any failure, so every non-zero exit code and signal-death status
    collapsed to 1, and a stray perl sat as the parent of every command
    and daemon. The generated mist.mistrc already runs perlbrew use, so
    the extra exec layer was redundant.

0.34 2014-05-26T19:30:01Z

  - Switch from linking to bash exec wrapper in perl5/{bin,sbin,script}

0.33 2014-04-30T16:04:04Z

  - Fixed install-time environment for assertions

0.32 2014-03-30T00:30:16Z

  - Merge command of mist is now full-featured
    This includes using its mistfile to install the foreign distribution
		and merge this file into the local one

0.31 2014-03-29T17:16:27Z

  - Added --prove option to mpan-install tht runs tests after install
    Especially useful as: (best run this overnight, it might take ages)
		  ./mpan-install --prove --all-available-versions

0.30 2014-03-29T04:51:33Z

  - Full merging of prepend, notest and cpanfile requirements
    This finally gives use notest for prepend, keeps all version information
    even if it comes from different sources (e.g. prepend now uses version
    requirements from cpanfile if no other is given).
 
  - Display usage text and version info with ./mpan-install --help

0.29 2014-03-29T01:32:19Z

  - Removed all instances of PERLBREW_HOME, it is not needed for mist
  - Once again install one module at a time so requirements will be sorted
    out correctly
  - mist itself now respects active branch
  - include local::lib so that mist is now fully self-contained
	
  Changes to mpan-install:
  - Consistent handling of @ARGV
  - Added --all-available-versions
  - changed --perl to --perlbrew so it does not clash with cpanm's option
  - Now supports installing of single modules
  - perlbrew script once again supports --perlbrew=system to
    disable use of perlbrew altogether

0.28 2014-03-20T03:13:36Z

  - Default value for --branch can now be determined by git
  - EXPERIMENTAL: --parent for branches using cp's --link feature

0.27 2014-03-18T03:43:10Z

  - Fixes to notest option and merge command

0.26 2014-03-18T02:10:10Z

  - Create a mist-run script in project root that uses the current branch
  - Import libs useful for assert-blocks in mistfile:
    Devel::CheckBin, Devel::CheckLib, Devel::CheckCompiler, Probe::Perl

0.25 2014-03-17T23:55:39Z

  - Added support for --branch parameter to support multiple perl5 directories
